  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Caution",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "No Venerable is recorded for this era. An empty list is not a claim that none existed. Sources disagree on Early Antiquity Era versus Late Antiquity Era before the present age. The Chinese name for this era is uncited. This page states nothing about where the regional walls come from.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sources do not agree on the name of the age immediately before the present age.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "name-in-the-succession",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sources conflict:",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "name-in-the-succession",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "The question is open.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "name-in-the-succession",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "In the immemorial antiquity era, Verdant Great Sun, Ren Zu’s eldest son, climbs the layered sky until his fall.",
      "chapters": [
        371
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "the-legends-of-ren-zu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_verdant_great_sun",
        "char_ren_zu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In the immemorial antiquity era the sky had nine levels, named by colour: white heaven, red heaven, orange heaven, yellow heaven, green heaven, azure heaven, blue heaven, purple heaven, and black heaven.",
      "chapters": [
        371
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "the-nine-heavens",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Seven of those nine are gone. Red, orange, yellow, green, azure, blue, and purple heavens were destroyed; at a later recounting only white heaven and black heaven remained, alternating as day and night.",
      "chapters": [
        389
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "the-nine-heavens",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Who destroyed the seven is not settled in one voice:",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "the-nine-heavens",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sources conflict:",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "the-nine-heavens",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "The question is open.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "the-nine-heavens",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nine heavens fragments still matter to Gu Immortals. In the Central Continent, Gu Immortals discuss a grotto-heaven that absorbed a fragment of blue heaven, name the immemorial nine heavens again, and envy how precious such a fragment is for a grotto-heaven.",
      "chapters": [
        740
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "the-nine-heavens",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_nine_heavens_fragment",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "reg_central_continent"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Entering black heaven, and a third voice on who left only two heavens.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "black-heaven-journeys",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "A later stretch states that because of Ren Zu and his ten children, only black heaven and white heaven were left. Black heaven itself remains a place that can be entered and crossed.",
      "chapters": [
        1241
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "black-heaven-journeys",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_heaven_black_heaven"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Later Gu Immortals at Reverse Flow River weighing living characters against Ren Zu.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "reverse-flow-record",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_reverse_flow_river"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At Reverse Flow River, later Gu Immortals weigh living characters against Ren Zu: he failed at the last step when he tried to walk out from the front, and Ma Hong Yun and Zhao Lian Yun are watched as possible breakers of that record.",
      "chapters": [
        1282
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "reverse-flow-record",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ma_hong_yun",
        "char_zhao_lian_yun"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "What Heavenly Court foresees for the two surviving heavens.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "two-heavens-foreshadowed",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_heavenly_court"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Heavenly Court immortals foresee that after the five regions begin to fuse, the two immemorial heavens will start fusing as well.",
      "chapters": [
        2001
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "two-heavens-foreshadowed",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "A Legends of Ren Zu inset that shatters blue heaven in legend text, not a present-day war.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "blue-heaven-inside-the-legends",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_the_legends_of_ren_zu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan opens The Legends of Ren Zu, chapter four, section thirty, in which Blazing Glory Lightning Brilliance and Myriad Gold Wondrous Essence reach immemorial blue heaven, and lightning Gu shatters that blue heaven in the legend text.",
      "chapters": [
        2021
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "blue-heaven-inside-the-legends",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_blazing_glory_lightning_brilliance",
        "sys_myriad_gold_wondrous_essence_physique",
        "gu_lightning_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Black heaven and white heaven once their late change is underway.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "black-and-white-heaven-late",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Black heaven and white heaven are fusing together, and it grows more severe as their walls and dao marks change.",
      "chapters": [
        2220
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "black-and-white-heaven-late",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
